      "content": "Major platforms like X and Meta often fail to distinguish between satire and hate speech, leading to the removal of legitimate political commentary while allowing harmful misinformation to spread. They rely on opaque algorithms and human moderators who are frequently biased against conservative voices, resulting in a \"chilling effect\" on free speech. The industry standard is actually broken because it prioritizes corporate safety over democratic discourse, and we need to demand stricter, more transparent guidelines that protect political dissent while only banning actual incitement to violence.",
