      "content": "interesting... so you're saying the current approach is fundamentally flawed. if we wanted to build a platform that actually avoids that \"chilling effect\" and stays neutral, would you say we should lean more towards a \"free speech absolutist\" model where almost nothing gets flagged unless it's direct threats, or is there a more balanced way to do it that doesn't just end up favoring one political side over the other?",
